4. Formulas to explain during your presentation

- Turnaround Time (TAT) = Completion Time − Arrival Time
- Waiting Time (WT) = Turnaround Time − Burst Time
- Response Time (RT) = First CPU Start Time − Arrival Time

The key difference is that non-preemptive scheduling lets a selected process finish before choosing another, whereas preemptive scheduling can interrupt a running process when a higher-priority process arrives.

